## Summary

| Aspect | Finding |
|--------|---------|
| **Framework** | Pure vanilla TypeScript + DOM manipulation |
| **Size** | ~2,000 LOC in main.ts; 400 LOC CSS + HTML |
| **Core logic** | TinyMCE editor + CodeMirror source view + split-pane UI + theme config + live preview |
| **Dependencies** | TinyMCE (large), CodeMirror, @pantoken/* (canvas-theme-editor, tinymce, cdn, etc.) |
| **Browser safety** | ✅ @pantoken/canvas-theme-editor + @pantoken/cdn are browser-safe (no node:* imports) |
| **Porting approach** | Convert vanilla DOM chains to Vue lifecycle hooks, wrap TinyMCE in ClientOnly, extract composables for reusable logic |
| **Localization** | Follow CdnPickerPage pattern (i18n.json + docs/theme/{name}.ts + useData()) |
| **Build risk** | TinyMCE SSR failure at VitePress pre-render time (mitigate w/ ClientOnly + dynamic import) |

**Next steps for porting**: Create `CanvasRcePage.vue` with Vue lifecycle, ClientOnly wrapper for TinyMCE, extracted composables for split-pane + theme state, i18n setup, and markdown entry at `docs/guide/canvas-rce.md`.

